  "message": "I checked with toyota_mechanic: Diagnosis only — nothing was changed.\n\n**The gap:** When Toyota delegates a request to another role (e.g. \"ask accounting about...\"), the voice sidecar says nothing until that role finishes, sometimes minutes later. In the dashboard version, a spoken acknowledgment (\"let me check with accounting\") fires immediately on delegation — but the REPL/voice path never wires that hook up, so `--voice` users get silence instead. This is even called out as a known gap in a code comment, and no test covers it.\n\n**Suggested fix (not applied):** In `main.py`'s `repl` function, build `voice_io` before `build_toyota`, then pass `on_delegation=voice_io.speak` into it — reusing the existing `DashboardVoiceIO.speak` method, which is already the right shape. Also add a test exercising this path, since none currently exist.\n\nWant me to have the mechanic apply this fix for real (sandboxed, auto-tested, auto-applied only if tests pass)?",
